+# HUD Kit export plan
+
+Source: `design/figma/hud-kit.json` (Figma page **HUD Kit**, node `30:1`, last modified 2026-11-02).
+
+This plan covers every visual on the page. For each one it says whether we **build** it from
+Roblox UI objects or **export** it from Figma as an image. For exported images it also gives the
+export size, the sprite sheet (if any), and the ImageLabel setup in Roblox.
+
+## Ground rules
+
+### Export at 2x
+All UI is authored in offsets for a screen 1080 px tall. `UI/Screen.luau` adds a `UIScale` of
+`clamp(shortSide / 1080, 1, 2)`. On 1080p the scale is 1, on 4K it is 2, and it never goes below 1.
+So:
+
+- **Export every image at 2x its authored (Figma) size.** The image is then always drawn at or
+  below its native resolution, and stays sharp on 4K.
+- **Size every GuiObject in authored (1x) offsets**, e.g. `UDim2.fromOffset(32, 32)` for a 32 px
+  icon. Do not size things in 2x pixels. `ImageRectOffset`, `ImageRectSize` and `SliceCenter` are
+  the exception: they are in **image pixels** (2x), because they address the texture.
+- The one exception is **Glow**, which is exported at 1x. It is a 30 px blur with no detail, so
+  scaling it up loses nothing.
+
+### Roblox limits and conventions
+- Roblox downscales any upload larger than **1024 x 1024**. Every sheet below fits in that.
+- Export PNG with transparent background. Figma: Export → PNG → `2x`.
+- **Hide every `Note` text layer before exporting.** Several of them are *children* of the frames
+  being exported (Panel / Ornate, Slot / Empty, Profile Card, Progress Bar), so they would end up in
+  the image.
+- One-color images that get tinted in game (icons, touch prompts, slot, dot grid, glow) are
+  exported **pure white at 100% opacity**. The colour and opacity are set in Roblox with
+  `ImageColor3` / `ImageTransparency`. White × `ImageColor3` gives exactly the designer's colour.
+- Sprite sheet layout: cells sit on a grid with an **8 px transparent gap** between cells (in sheet
+  pixels), starting at (0, 0). The gap stops neighbouring cells bleeding in when the image is
+  filtered at fractional scales. Offsets for column `c`, row `r` are
+  `(c × (cell + 8), r × (cell + 8))`.
+- Common ImageLabel properties for every image below (not repeated in each section):
+  `BackgroundTransparency = 1`, `BorderSizePixel = 0`, `ResampleMode = Enum.ResamplerMode.Default`.
+  `ScaleType = Stretch` unless stated otherwise.
+- Font everywhere is Builder Sans: `Font.new("rbxasset://fonts/families/BuilderSans.json", weight)`
+  with `Enum.FontWeight.Regular` / `Bold` / `ExtraBold` as listed.
+
