+## Built from Roblox UI objects
+
+### Prompts / Keyboard (`40:129`) — build
+Rounded key cap with a text label. Everything here maps to native objects, and live text keeps it
+sharp at any scale and lets us add keys without new art.
+
+Figma draws the 2 px stroke **inside** the 40 px box. `UIStroke` draws **outside** the frame, so
+shrink the frame by the stroke on each side to keep the same outer size:
+
+| Object | Properties |
+|---|---|
+| `Frame` "KeyPrompt" | `Size = UDim2.fromOffset(36, 36)` (B, I, E, Q, 1, 2, 3) or `fromOffset(52, 36)` (Esc, Tab, Shift); `BackgroundColor3 = 235,237,242` |
+| └ `UICorner` | `CornerRadius = UDim.new(0, 4)` (4 inner + 2 stroke = Figma's 6 outer) |
+| └ `UIStroke` | `Thickness = 2`, `Color = 153,157,171`, `ApplyStrokeMode = Border` |
+| └ `TextLabel` "Label" | `Size = UDim2.fromScale(1, 1)`, `BackgroundTransparency = 1`, Builder Sans **Bold**, `TextSize = 18`, `TextColor3 = 31,33,41`, centred both ways, `Text` = `B` / `I` / `E` / `Q` / `1` / `2` / `3` / `Esc` / `Tab` / `Shift` |
+
+Note: "Shift" at 18 px bold is about as wide as the 40 px label area in Figma. Use
+`TextScaled = false` and check it doesn't clip; if it does, widen that key rather than shrinking the
+text.
+
+### Card / Ribbon (`40:141`) — build
+240 x 56, colour 222,67,82, with "NEW" in white. Its corners are uneven
+(`rectangleCornerRadii [16, 0, 16, 0]` = top-left 16, top-right 0, bottom-right 16, bottom-left 0).
+`UICorner` rounds all four corners, so square off the other two with filler frames:
+
+| Object | Properties |
+|---|---|
+| `Frame` "Ribbon" | `Size = fromOffset(240, 56)`, `BackgroundColor3 = 222,67,82` |
+| └ `UICorner` | `CornerRadius = UDim.new(0, 16)` |
+| └ `Frame` "SquareTR" | `AnchorPoint = (1, 0)`, `Position = fromScale(1, 0)`, `Size = fromOffset(16, 16)`, same colour, no corner |
+| └ `Frame` "SquareBL" | `AnchorPoint = (0, 1)`, `Position = fromScale(0, 1)`, `Size = fromOffset(16, 16)`, same colour, no corner |
+| └ `TextLabel` "Label" | `Size = fromScale(1, 1)`, `ZIndex` above the squares, Builder Sans **ExtraBold**, `TextSize = 22`, white, centred, `Text = "NEW"` |
+
+### Profile Card (`40:153`) — build; avatar is a runtime image
+- Card: `Frame` 360 x 190, `BackgroundColor3 = 33,37,54`, `UICorner` 16.
+- **Avatar: do not export.** The Note says the photo is a placeholder for the player's headshot.
+  Use an `ImageLabel` at `Position = fromOffset(20, 20)`, `Size = fromOffset(150, 150)`,
+  `Image` = the result of
+  `Players:GetUserThumbnailAsync(userId, Enum.ThumbnailType.HeadShot, Enum.ThumbnailSize.Size420x420)`
+  (420 rather than 150, so it holds up at 2x = 300 px), plus `UICorner` with
+  `CornerRadius = UDim.new(0.5, 0)` to make it a circle.
+
+### Glass Card (`40:155`) — build, blur dropped
+Roblox cannot blur what is behind a 2D GuiObject. `BlurEffect` only blurs the 3D world and has no
+mask. So we build the tint and border and leave out the background blur:
+
+| Object | Properties |
+|---|---|
+| `Frame` "GlassCard" | `Size = fromOffset(318, 198)` (inside stroke, as for the key caps), `BackgroundColor3 = 255,255,255`, `BackgroundTransparency = 0.9` |
+| └ `UICorner` | `CornerRadius = UDim.new(0, 15)` |
+| └ `UIStroke` | `Thickness = 1`, white, `Transparency = 0.8`, `ApplyStrokeMode = Border` |
+| └ `TextLabel` "Title" | `Position = fromOffset(23, 19)`, Builder Sans **Bold**, `TextSize = 22`, white, left-aligned, `Text = "Inventory"` |
+
+**Designer sign-off needed:** if the blur matters, the only option is a `Lighting.BlurEffect` turned
+on while the menu is open. That blurs the whole 3D view, not only the area behind the card.
+
+### Progress Bar (`40:158`) — build
+| Object | Properties |
+|---|---|
+| `Frame` "Track" | `Size = fromOffset(300, 12)`, white, `BackgroundTransparency = 0.88`, `UICorner` 6 |
+| └ `Frame` "Fill" | `Size = UDim2.new(progress, 0, 1, 0)` (from quest progress, 0–1), `BackgroundColor3 = 87,209,118`, `UICorner` 6 |
+
+Set `Fill.Visible = false` at 0 progress. Below 12 px wide the rounded ends squash together.
