+### 10. `ItemPortrait_<Name>` — Item Portraits (`40:150`), one file each
+120 portraits, growing every update, shown **one at a time** in the item detail pane at 128 x 128.
+A sheet would make the player download every portrait to see one, and every new item would mean
+re-packing the sheet. So each portrait is its own upload.
+
+- Export each `Item Portrait/<Name>` rectangle at **2x → 256 x 256**, rounded 12 px corners baked
+  in. Name the file `ItemPortrait_<Name>.png` (e.g. `ItemPortrait_Torch.png`).
+- The page only has 6 of the 120 (Torch, Ladder, Door, Fence, Chest, Bed). The other 114 follow the
+  same spec.
+- These are raster image fills (`scaleMode FILL`). Check that each source image is at least
+  256 x 256, or the 2x export is just an upscale.
+- ImageLabel: `Image = ItemPortrait_<Name>`, `Size = fromOffset(128, 128)`. No `UICorner` needed.
